{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"ac86c2b7d1e32f2e42cca91746c35f2282840da7567cdea0610bc4aa71465a19","digest":{"component_or_area":"mutation sandbox hardening","key_entities":["docs/local-dev-env.md","docs/mutation-testing.md","scripts/mutation_gate.py","scripts/mutation_sandbox.py","mutation_sandbox.wrap()","execute_shard","sandbox_allow","sys.prefix","CI environment variable","Seatbelt profile","allow-list","bwrap --bind"],"problem_keywords":["sandbox documentation mismatch","missing path handling","fail-open condition","security posture disclosure","mutation testing","observability"],"propositions":["Documentation in docs/local-dev-env.md incorrectly describes the venv as writable inside the sandbox; the shipped allow-list deliberately excludes sys.prefix from sandbox_allow to prevent mutant code execution.","Missing allow-list paths are silently skipped with bare continue rather than surfaced as warnings, causing confusing write failures inside the sandbox with no indication of the root cause.","The CI fail-open runs unsandboxed when CI is set but lacks warning clarity about the variable name and value, making the unsandboxed state indistinguishable from a normal run in logs.","The Seatbelt profile restricts writes only via (allow default) + (deny file-write*), leaving reads and network unrestricted, without documented reasoning for this security posture."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787910136906668001,"uuid":"2b0db644-9c70-4478-a649-84bf8f9e6f0a"}